From c790e832b1152d44097dd91b01ef6159a1113a1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:37:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: level 5 offsets that say bars where the picture has
 content are measured and left aside

The other wrong level 5 block (an "open matte" encode with the RPU of
the letterboxed one, a picture cropped on both axes from its master)
fits a reading of the picture, and native output blanked the rows of
the picture that it calls bars. Whether it does is now measured on a
few pictures of the video, with the measurement of the bridge that HDR10
measured as Dolby Vision uses (dvbridge_measure.c, in an instance of its
own, and dvbridge_measured_reduce(): the rows and columns that hold
blocks above its black level), and decided over several of them, never
on one (dvbridge_l5check.h).

Which pictures: only of native output, only while the offsets make bars
inside the picture (dvbridge_candidate_picture_bars()), only P010
surfaces (what the measurement reads), not a picture that stands still
and not one whose metadata Hades makes (HDR10 measured, HDR10+ sent as
Dolby Vision). Of those, one a second in the first 10 s of the video,
then one at a cut of its RPU (scene_refresh_flag) at most every 10 s,
and one every 30 s without a cut: in a two hour video with a cut every
3 s, 609 pictures of 172800 (simulated). The other pictures ask nothing
of the GPU: what is measured is collected without waiting at a later
frame, with one glClientWaitSync() while a measurement is in flight and
no GL call at all while none is (read in the code). A measured picture
costs two small passes over its 2x2 blocks and a read back through a
fence: 11 ms of wall clock for a 4K picture on lavapipe, a software
renderer (submit and glFinish), and 0.2 ms of processor for the submit.

The decision: three measured pictures with content in more than half of
a bar of 8 samples or more (dvbridge_dv_l5_contradicted(), moved here),
the first and the last at least 2 s apart. A dark scene, a black
opening, or a few bright rows at the edge of a bar contradict nothing;
one picture does not decide. Then the offsets are left aside for the
rest of the video (dvbridge_dv_ignore_l5_of(), of the video of the
picture, which is drawn before its measurement comes back), nothing
more is measured of it, and a renderer made again within the video
takes the decision again (CDVBridgeGLES::Cm40Video(), as the decision of
the content mapping v4.0 is kept).

Tested on the host with real pictures of the FEL test stream on zink
over lavapipe (a host test, l5gpu_test.c): its own offsets (bars of
275 and 276 rows, black) after a black and a nearly black opening, the
same with three bright rows at the edge of the top bar, and one picture
filled into its bars among right ones: never left aside; offsets of 600
rows, and the pictures filled into their bars with the stream's own
offsets ("open matte"): left aside after three measured pictures. Two
mutations of dvbridge_l5check.h each make it fail: deciding on one
picture, and any content in a bar contradicting.

kodi.log: "DVBridge: the level 5 offsets of this video make bars of
l r t b samples (left, right, top, bottom) in its WxH picture, and N of
the M pictures measured have content there (a s to b s; the last one in
rows ... and columns ...): they are left aside for the rest of the
video", then the bridge's own line "DVBridge: the level 5 offsets of
this video (...) cannot describe its picture: measured pictures have
content where they say bars. ..." once.
